@sidharthv96, is removing this `throw e;` line in https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/pull/4359/commits/16c12a42c7892eb268e4afdc9e9cf589ce9138a4 the expected behavior?

It seems like currently, the `mermaid.render()` function will render an error diagram, then throw an exception if the `diag.renderer.draw` function fails.

But now, it will only do that if `suppressErrorRendering: true`.

Would something like the following be better, since then by default, the behavior would be the same?

```ts
if (config.suppressErrorRendering) {
  removeTempElements();
} else {
  errorRenderer.draw(text, id, version);
}
throw e;
```

I'm getting a race-condition when running the E2E test. The following seems to fix it:

```suggestion
      cy.get('#test').find("svg").should(($svg) => {
        expect($svg).to.have.length(2); // all failing diagrams should not appear!
        $svg.each((_index, svg) => {
          expect(cy.$$(svg)).to.be.visible;

          // none of the diagrams should be error diagrams
          expect($svg).to.not.contain("Syntax error");
        });
      });
```

### See screenshot of before and after:

![configuration spec-should-not-render-error-diagram-if-suppressErrorRendering-is-set diff](https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/assets/19716675/61d57753-6e8e-4f78-b056-7d0aa30f2690)

I'm getting a race-condition when running the E2E test. The following seems to fix it:

```suggestion
      cy.get('#test').find("svg").should(($svg) => {
        expect($svg).to.have.length(5); // all five diagrams should be rendered!
        $svg.each((_index, svg) => {
          expect(cy.$$(svg)).to.be.visible;
        });

        // some of the diagrams should be error diagrams
        expect($svg).to.contain("Syntax error");
      });
```

